// A regular function call (not operator syntax) never compiles to `CallVec`,
// even when the argument is a tuple: vec dispatch is gated to operator syntax
// via the `OperatorCall` AST variant. `id((1, 2, 3))` puts `id` in r1 and the
// tuple `MakeTuple` makes in r2, then `Call r1, 1`.
// compile: stdlib
fn id(x) { x }; id((1, 2, 3))
